# TestNullabilityOracleGuava.inference(): the NULL_MARKED policy's TOTAL row, guava's verdicts scored against guava's
# own JSpecify annotations (CodeLaser/maddi-mod#51). `unsafe` (non-null where guava says nullable) is a hard ceiling:
# any change fails, and a lower value is written here in the commit that earns it. `noise` (nullable where guava's
# context guarantees a value) is the trend number: it fails only when it moves more than `noiseSlack` either way. The
# other three policies and the per-kind, per-depth rows are logged, not ratcheted.
#
# Machine and input matter: until the guava input configuration was refreshed on 2026-10-13, the Mac and laser1
# measured different numbers. Record on laser1, and say so when a number comes from elsewhere.
#
# 2026-10-25, first record, devel at maddi afb4537bf / maddi-mod 187d3281: 336 unsafe, 1,736 noise, 275 undecided, on
# laser1 and on the Mac alike (10-13: 341, 1,740), after some 80 verdict commits for the Java -> Kotlin translation.
#
# 2026-10-26, devel at maddi a147b75f1 / maddi-mod 4b6c7a68, measured on the Mac: 234 unsafe, 1,834 noise, 274
# undecided. #68 (a parameter that tolerates null prints nullable) and its overload and override rules: 114 parameters
# that guava annotates @Nullable now agree, and 98 more read nullable where guava's context guarantees a value.
#
# 2026-10-26, devel at maddi f2cae7ece / maddi-mod b0cd2a7c, measured on the Mac: 229 unsafe, 1,834 noise. An unread
# parameter loses its tolerance only when the method has an analysed override: StringCatcher's and the four
# NullPointerTesterTest.OneArg parameters agree again.
#
# 2026-10-28, devel at maddi 71f1bf3b2 / maddi-mod 7c4e53f4, on laser1: 230 unsafe, 1,834 noise, 274 undecided.
# Accepted by Bart. The one new unsafe row is guava's test class eventbus.StringCatcher.hereHaveAString(@Nullable
# String string), which only does `events.add(string)` into a private List<String>. maddi-mod 7d05682c stops a
# tolerated null at a field's element slot (gate NOTOLERANTSLOTS), so that public adders and setters stop printing
# @Nullable. Guava's own declaration is inconsistent here: a @Nullable String goes into a List<String> in null-marked
# code.
unsafe	230
noise	1834
noiseSlack	20
